    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 12 with a primary offensive engine fueled by **Yordan Alvarez** (85.82), whose elite xwOBA of 0.465 against a vulnerable Houser makes him our highest-projected asset today. He is closely followed by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.99), who earns a significant boost from an aggressive 6.75 xERA matchup against Kent, J, despite a platoon disadvantage. **Junior Caminero** (69.54) also profiles as a core play, benefiting from a +10% park factor and a premium #3 spot in the order. In the outfield, **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) presents an underrated opportunity; while his base projection is modest, his +19% SP skill advantage against Feltner and a favorable platoon matchup yield the highest ceiling outside of our Tier-1 producers.\n\nStrategic roster optimization reveals a tight margin at the margins, with **Pedro Ramirez** (54.35) serving as our strongest bench contingency. **Pedro Ramirez** surged due to the same favorable matchup against Kent, J that boosted **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, but his lower spot in the batting order ultimately suppressed his scoring relative to our starting options. We are also monitoring the SB profile closely; while **Caleb Durbin** (55.87) and **Trea Turner** (58.78) face slightly tougher pitching environments, their ability to swipe bases remains the anchor of our daily strategy. We have successfully avoided the drag of **Colt Keith**, who remains sidelined, ensuring our active slots are fully optimized for efficiency. Risks are currently concentrated on the platoon-heavy profiles of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Gary Sanchez**, though both are deemed start-worthy given the weakness of the opposing arms on the mound today.",
